camfr3
======

camfr3 is a Python 3 port of CAMFR (CAvity Modelling FRamework). It is
distributed under the name "camfr3" because the PyPI name "camfr" belongs to
the original author. The Python module is still imported as "camfr".

CAMFR was written by Peter Bienstman at the Photonics Research Group,
Department of Information Technology (INTEC), Ghent University, Belgium,
with contributions from the people listed in AUTHORS.

    Copyright (C) 1998-2007 Peter Bienstman - Ghent University

Original project:  http://camfr.sourceforge.net/
Upstream fork:     https://github.com/demisjohn/CAMFR

The Python 3 port (branch python3-port) is maintained by
Abdelfettah Hadij-ElHouati. Every change made for the port is documented in
PORTING_JOURNAL.md.

If you use this software in published work, please cite:

    P. Bienstman and R. Baets, "Optical modelling of photonic crystals and
    VCSELs using eigenmode expansion and perfectly matched layers",
    Optical and Quantum Electronics 33, 327-341 (2001).
    doi:10.1023/A:1010882531238

