camfr/math/ contains third-party numerical code:

- The SLATEC Bessel routines (camfr/math/bessel/slatec/): US government
  work, public domain. Some of them were also published as ACM algorithms
  (e.g. D. E. Amos, TOMS Algorithm 644); the copies here are SLATEC's.
  SLATEC's machine constants (d1mach) come from Fortran intrinsics; the
  MACHAR routine (W. J. Cody, ACM TOMS 14, 1988) that computed them was
  removed (PORTING_JOURNAL.md, entry 58).

- Brent's root finder and minimiser (camfr/math/calculus/root/,
  minimum/): adapted from Oleg Kiselyov's Numerical Math Class Library,
  which its author placed in the public domain ("All the code is in Public
  Domain", https://okmij.org/ftp/NumMath.html).

